module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_namespace_root_segment_resolves_as_a_bare_reference

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data a_namespace_root_segment_resolves_as_a_bare_reference: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_namespace_root_segment_resolves_as_a_bare_reference" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "a namespace root segment resolves as a bare reference: the first segment of a qualified module path -- `v2` in `v2.std.node.Node` -- is classified as a free value reference, and because the pool happens to declare something with that spelling it resolves to that declaration. The reference-derived dependency producer then publishes an edge from the reading module into a module it never names. Nothing refuses: the edge is well formed, the closure it widens still resolves, and every consumer of the closure reads a larger population as the true one.",

    "SPECIMEN, found 2026-09-23 by the Pkg7e emitted-workspace plan (v2.workflow.emitted_crate_workspace), whose two-closure join refused with ClosuresDisagree: the live dependency DAG of v2.compiler.compile carried 214 modules, the seed's emission 190, and the 24 extra included test.claim.secret_rotation_witness. That test module declares `fn v2()`. Every import-free production module reading a `v2.std.*` path -- src/v2/std/artifact, src/v2/std/grounding, src/v2/std/cross_tree/resolution among them -- gained a UniqueBare edge into it, and its imports pulled in the rest.",

    "THE EARLIEST UNJUSTIFIED LINK (DESIGN section 6b), found by walking the producer from its output back: v1_compiler.cli_run ExprVarClassification classify decided that a dotted chain's head is a namespace segment only when NO declaration anywhere shares its spelling, and reference_resolution_facts runs with no declaration index at all, so that arm could never fire there and every head fell to the free-reference default. The dotted scan had already recorded the chain whole and resolved it Qualified by longest_declared_module_prefix; the head's role was a fact the producer held and did not consult. The repair classifies a head whose chain names a declared module as QualifiedChainHead, the member it always belonged to; only a binder outranks it, and a dotted read whose head names no module (a value row's field) keeps its edge.",

    "RUNG: mechanically preventable. test.claim.namespace_root_reference_edge_witness runs the real producer over fixtures/namespace_root_homonym, where nsroot_decl.homonym declares fn nsroot() beside the nsroot.pkg.* modules: the RED asserts no consumer edge to the homonym and FAILED on the unrepaired binary; the control asserts the qualified edge and a value-chain edge both survive. The corpus-scale control is the Pkg7e plan's closure join, which admits only when the live DAG and the emission are the same population.",

    "THE SECOND ARM OF THE SAME CLASS, found by the same plan once the first was repaired: the live DAG still carried std.string_type, because import-free dag/std/primitives annotates `data primitive_contract_roster_note: String` and the producer resolved the kernel spelling String UniqueBare to the nearest module declaring it. The resolver never binds a kernel or container spelling to a module; that rule already had one home, the census pull's substrate-vocabulary skip, and it is now the named v1_compiler.cli_run is_substrate_vocabulary that both producers read. RED a_kernel_type_spelling_never_resolves_to_a_declaring_module over fixtures/substrate_vocabulary_edge FAILED on the binary without it and PASSES with it; its control keeps an ordinary type's edge. The shared shape of both arms is the recognition rule: the reference producer binding a name to a module that the resolver's own precedence says the name never binds to.",

    "ATTAINABLE CEILING: structurally guaranteed. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, at capability grain: the namespace-cut terminal step (docs/plans/namespace-cut-replacement-plan.md), where dependencies are parse-then-derive from resolved container.member references rather than classified occurrences -- sufficient for a qualified path to reach the dependency graph only as a resolved module identity, so no segment of it is ever looked up as a bare name.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
